Subject: kcc: KccSkipCanvasPerfSampling - never sample canvas render tasks for UMA

Stock behaviour
---------------
third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/canvas_performance_monitor.cc,
CanvasPerformanceMonitor::CurrentTaskDrawsToContext(): the first canvas draw
of a main-thread task registers the monitor as a TaskTimeObserver and decides
whether the task is "measured":

  static constexpr int kSamplingProbabilityInv = 100;
  measure_current_task_ = !(task_counter_++ % kSamplingProbabilityInv);

so the 1st, 101st, 201st... task that draws to any canvas is sampled. At the
end of a sampled task, DidProcessTask() calls RecordMetrics(), which starts
with

  size_t partition_alloc_kb = Partitions::TotalActiveBytes() / kKiloByte;

Partitions::TotalActiveBytes() (platform/wtf/allocator/partitions.cc) is
  LightPartitionStatsDumperImpl dumper;
  Partitions::DumpMemoryStats(true, &dumper);
i.e. PartitionRoot::DumpStats() over the fast_malloc, array_buffer and buffer
partitions (takes each root's lock and walks its buckets/slot spans). The
result, ProcessHeap::TotalAllocatedObjectSize() and the task duration are
then written to dynamically named Blink.Canvas.* / Blink.OffscreenCanvas.*
UMA histograms (one StrCat + histogram lookup each). Nothing else consumes
the values.

In a trace of the game this is CanvasPerformanceMonitor::RecordMetrics at
0.64 ms mean / 1.28 ms max on every 100th frame: at 1000 FPS a one-frame
hitch ten times a second, for metrics this build never uploads.

Change
------
New feature KccSkipCanvasPerfSampling (file-local, disabled by default). When
enabled, measure_current_task_ is always false, so no task is ever sampled
and RecordMetrics() never runs.

Cut point: only the sampling decision. I read the whole monitor and its
callers (CanvasRenderingContext::DidDraw is the only caller of
CurrentTaskDrawsToContext; DidDraw(DrawType) is also called from
OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D). All state in the class
(rendering_context_descriptions_, draw_types_, call_type_, task_counter_,
is_render_task_, measure_current_task_) is private and read only by the
metrics code, so an early return at the top of CurrentTaskDrawsToContext
would also have been safe and would additionally save the per-task
Add/RemoveTaskTimeObserver. I deliberately did not do that: with this cut
every render task takes exactly the path that 99 of 100 tasks already take
in stock (observer added, is_render_task_ set, DidProcessTask removes the
observer and clears draw_types_), so there is no new state combination to
reason about. The canvas frame-push logic (CanvasRenderingContext's own
TaskObserver, did_draw_in_current_task_) is separate and untouched.

The feature is read once into a function-local static; the read sits after
the existing IsMainThread() early return, so it is only ever evaluated on
the main thread. With the feature disabled the expression is
!false && !(task_counter_++ % 100), i.e. stock, including the counter
increment.

Gating / A-B
------------
--enable-features=KccSkipCanvasPerfSampling (renderer process).
Measure: in a trace with the "blink" category,
CanvasPerformanceMonitor::RecordMetrics slices must disappear; frame-time
1%/0.1% lows and the every-100th-frame spike in a frame-time plot.

Platforms: all (no OS-specific code).

Side effects when enabled: the Blink.Canvas.*.RenderTaskDuration.*,
*.PartitionAlloc.* and *.BlinkGC.* histograms (and the OffscreenCanvas
equivalents) are no longer recorded. No test under
third_party/blink/renderer references those histogram names (grep), and the
default is off in any case.

Not verified: not compiled.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/canvas_performance_monitor.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/canvas_performance_monitor.cc
index 413283b18259dd13c6dc9b0933d8dd1c20a78a19..80b5e1327206bc03af76c06a2dd42ed938954464 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/canvas_performance_monitor.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/canvas_performance_monitor.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/canvas_performance_monitor.h"
 
+#include "base/feature_list.h"
 #include "base/metrics/histogram_functions.h"
 #include "base/metrics/histogram_macros.h"
 #include "base/trace_event/trace_event.h"
@@ -48,6 +49,11 @@ const char* const kMeasurementName_BlinkGC = ".BlinkGC";
 // measured.
 static constexpr int kSamplingProbabilityInv = 100;
 
+// KCC: when enabled, no render task is ever sampled, so RecordMetrics() (and
+// its walk of the PartitionAlloc heaps) never runs. Everything else the
+// monitor does per render task is left exactly as for an unsampled task.
+BASE_FEATURE(kKccSkipCanvasPerfSampling, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+
 // Encodes and decodes information about a CanvasRenderingContext as a
 // 32-bit value.
 class RenderingContextDescriptionCodec {
@@ -151,7 +157,10 @@ void CanvasPerformanceMonitor::CurrentTaskDrawsToContext(
     // the metrics must be executed exactly once per render task to avoid
     // sampling biases that would skew metrics for cases that render to multiple
     // canvases per render task.
-    measure_current_task_ = !(task_counter_++ % kSamplingProbabilityInv);
+    static const bool kcc_skip_sampling =
+        base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kKccSkipCanvasPerfSampling);
+    measure_current_task_ =
+        !kcc_skip_sampling && !(task_counter_++ % kSamplingProbabilityInv);
 
     if (!measure_current_task_) [[likely]] {
       return;
